@page "/roof-tune-up-charlotte-nc"
@{
    ViewData["Lang"] = "en";
    ViewData["SeoEn"] = "/roof-tune-up-charlotte-nc";
    ViewData["SeoEs"] = "/es/mantenimiento-de-techo-charlotte-nc";
}
<main class="resource-site" lang="en">
    @await Html.PartialAsync("_SeoIntentHeader")
    <section class="resource-hero systems-hero">
        <div class="site-shell">
            <p class="eyebrow eyebrow-light">$350 Roof Tune-Up</p>
            <h1>$350 Roof Tune-Up in Charlotte, NC</h1>
            <p>A general annual maintenance visit for accessible roof areas: visual review, sealant at exposed fasteners and penetrations, chimney water-entry details and notes on visible concerns. It is not a replacement, not a leak repair and not a claim result.</p>
            <div class="hero-actions">
                <a class="button button-gold" href="#contact">Request a Tune-Up</a>
                <a class="button button-ghost" href="/faqs">Roofing FAQs</a>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>
    <section class="resource-body section" id="process">
        <div class="site-shell resource-sections">
            <article><span>01</span><div>
                <h2>What the $350 visit includes</h2>
                <p>Accessible roof review, maintenance caulking or sealant at exposed fasteners and penetrations, chimney water-entry details, and a review for visible roof concerns. Hidden damage, decking, structural work, interior repairs and replacement are separate scopes.</p>
            </div></article>
            <article><span>02</span><div>
                <h2>When a Tune-Up is not enough</h2>
                <p>Active leaks, open holes, missing shingles after wind or widespread storm patterns need a repair or inspection path instead. Start with <a class="official-link" href="/roof-repair-charlotte-nc">repair</a>, <a class="official-link" href="/emergency-roof-repair-charlotte-nc">emergency tarping</a> or a <a class="official-link" href="/free-roof-inspection-charlotte-nc">free storm inspection</a>.</p>
            </div></article>
            <article><span>03</span><div>
                <h2>Annual maintenance, not a storm response</h2>
                <p>Schedule a Tune-Up when the roof is generally performing and you want accessible sealing details reviewed. After hail, wind, a tree strike or an active leak, use <a class="official-link" href="/repair-or-replace-roof">repair vs replace</a> or a <a class="official-link" href="/free-roof-inspection-charlotte-nc">free inspection</a> instead.</p>
            </div></article>
        </div>
    </section>
    <section class="faq-section section" id="faq">
        <div class="site-shell faq-layout">
            <div><p class="eyebrow">FAQ</p><h2>Tune-Up questions</h2></div>
            <div class="faq-list">
                <details><summary>Is the Tune-Up a full roof replacement?<span>+</span></summary><p>No. It is maintenance on accessible areas. A replacement is a different project with a written construction scope.</p></details>
                <details><summary>Does the Tune-Up include interior repairs?<span>+</span></summary><p>No. Interior work, decking, structural items and hidden conditions require a separate agreement.</p></details>
                <details><summary>Do you serve Raleigh for Tune-Ups?<span>+</span></summary><p>No. Availability is confirmed by address within about 90 minutes of Charlotte, NC or Rock Hill, SC.</p></details>
                <details><summary>Will a Tune-Up stop an active leak?<span>+</span></summary><p>No. An active leak, open hole or widespread storm damage needs repair, tarping or inspection—not maintenance alone.</p></details>
                <details><summary>How often is a Tune-Up recommended?<span>+</span></summary><p>It is planned as a general annual maintenance visit, not as a storm-response service.</p></details>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>
    @await Html.PartialAsync("_SeoIntentFooter")
</main>
